  "script": "Hitler's Eagle's Nest in the Alps burned on Friday night. Around two hundred firefighters fought the blaze, Reuters reported. The house sits on a cliff, more than eighteen hundred meters up. It was finished in nineteen thirty-eight and survived World War Two undamaged. Here's what's at risk now. Since nineteen fifty-two, it's been a restaurant with a history exhibit. No one was hurt. But tourism officials say it's not clear if parts can be saved. What should happen to the site? Tell us below.",
